+## A-LOWER — finite packing lower estimate
+
+Hypotheses: `n` is beyond the construction threshold and the frozen extremal
+function ranges over finite one-separated subsets of three-space. Inference:
+take a nearly cubical finite fragment of the face-centred-cubic packing, count
+interior contacts, and bound the boundary loss by `c₁ n^(2/3)`. Output:
+`6 n - c₁ n^(2/3) ≤ f 3 n` eventually. Formal anchor: proof node
+`N-LOWER` and the lower premise consumed by `compose_eventual_bounds`.
+Downstream use: `N-COMPOSE`. Exceptional cases: small `n`, rounding of the
+finite fragment, and incomplete boundary shells are absorbed by the eventual
+threshold and enlargement of `c₁`. Trust boundary: the quantitative finite
+count must be replayed from reviewed theorem bodies; the source conjecture is
+not evidence for it.
+
+## A-UPPER — quantitative contact upper estimate
+
+Hypotheses: an arbitrary finite one-separated configuration of `n` points in
+three-space, with `n` beyond the contact theorem threshold. Inference: replace
+points by disjoint radius-one-half balls, identify unit-distance pairs with
+tangencies, and apply the quantitative three-dimensional contact-number
+inequality, including its positive surface-deficit constant. Output: for some
+`c₂ > 0`, `f 3 n ≤ 6 n - c₂ n^(2/3)` eventually. Formal anchor: proof node
+`N-UPPER` and the upper premise consumed by `compose_eventual_bounds`.
+Downstream use: `N-COMPOSE`. Exceptional cases: coincident points are excluded
+by separation; finite small configurations are covered by the eventual
+threshold; zero is outside the asymptotic branch. Trust boundary: Master must
+identify and replay the exact reviewed quantitative contact theorem and every
+transitive dependency at trust zero.
+
+## A-COMPOSE — eventual root composition
+
+Hypotheses: the eventual lower estimate, the eventual upper estimate, and
+positivity of the chosen upper constant. Inference: intersect the two tails of
+`atTop`, retain both inequalities, and introduce `c₁` and `c₂` in the frozen
+quantifier order. Output: the exact frozen existential/eventual conjunction.
+Formal anchor:
+`AwesomeTheorems.Stage5.S5_CLM_00003661.compose_eventual_bounds` and the
+claim-owned exact wrapper. Downstream use: machine closure, semantic audit,
+and provisional release. Exceptional cases: differing thresholds are replaced
+by their maximum; neither conjunct nor positivity may be dropped. Trust
+boundary: only the local logical composition is represented directly in this
+worker surface; canonical Master must verify that the independently compiled
+lower and upper bodies close the exact unconditional root.
